  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AAU &amp; JU 2016-2025,  CSO uppdragsutbildning</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AAU &amp; JU 2016-2025, CSO leadership training Commission education - AAU &amp; JU Commission education scheme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering fr&#xe5;n Sida om 28 miljoner f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra programmet &quot;AAU uppdragsutbildningsprogram&quot;. Insatsen avser utveckla och leverera ett fem&#xe5;rigt kapacitets-uppbyggnads program f&#xf6;r chefer och mellanchefer inom etiopiska civila samh&#xe4;llsorganisationer, genom ett uppdragsutbildningsprogram inom AAU/JU. Insatsen &#xe4;r relevant i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till den svenska regeringens strategier f&#xf6;r Etiopien 2016-2020 samt f&#xf6;r forskningssamarbetet och strategin f&#xf6;r forskning inom utvecklingssamarbete 2015-2021. AAU samarbetar med J&#xf6;nk&#xf6;pings Universitet (JU), och en del av de beg&#xe4;rda medlen kommer att g&#xe5; till JU. AAU har varit en Sida-partner under en l&#xe5;ng tid och de uppfyller lagkravet f&#xf6;r att ing&#xe5; avtal. Organisationen har intern kapacitet att hantera projektet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project introduces a Commission Education scheme with Addis Ababa University which serves primarily the civil society organisations     operating in Ethiopia through provision of tailor made professional   and skills training.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the program is to increase the capacity of AAU and Ethiopian civil society organisation to cooperate and exchange experience with partners in the Ethiopian society. 
The project had two specific objectives to contribute to the realisation of the overall objective. 

These are;
1. To increase the capacity at AAU to meet Ethiopian development priorities by
providing tailor-made services to private/public and civil society organisation
active in Ethiopia. In the last phase of the project (July 2023-December 2024), this objective was broadened to include leadership training of the faculty members at the School of economics and AAU at large. 
2. To increase the capacity among leaders in Ethiopian civil society organisations to further develop and sustain the CSOs through a more reflective, inclusive, and participatory leadership practice. 

CED&apos;s leadership program is different from conventional management training programs, that have been rather focusing on technical aspects of running the organization such as book keeping, project planning and monitoring. CED&apos;s program aims are to go beyond the technical aspects towards a transformational mode, through the fostering of creative, motivated, and dynamic leaders who in turn manage staff (that produce the expected outputs and outcomes) efficiently and effectively from a human rights-based approach.

The methodology produces the expected outcomes and outputs.</narrative>
  </description>
